  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": "Docker Engine 29.10.0; Docker Compose v5.8.0; Dockerfile reference and Compose Specification checked 2026-11-20",
      "items": [
        "Docker Engine 29.10.0 (released 2026-11-16) adds opt-in experimental daemon-managed one-shot/scheduled jobs, an OpenAPI 3.2 Engine API source specification, customizable embedded containerd configuration, a `restarting` die-event attribute, and changed handling of loopback registries when insecure-registries is explicitly configured. The jobs extension is disabled by default; its gRPC API is served on daemon listener addresses and Docker authorization plugins do not authorize it.",
        "Docker Compose v5.8.0 (released 2026-11-17) adds manual and scheduled top-level jobs. Scheduled jobs require Docker Engine 29.10+ with its experimental jobs extension enabled. Jobs remain experimental; scheduled runs do not start or wait for depends_on dependencies. Compose Specification keys have per-field minimum versions; validate with the installed docker compose version and docker compose config.",
        "Current Dockerfile reference includes instruction modifiers beyond the basic instruction names: COPY/ADD flags, labs-only FROM --reset and configuration --unset features, and BuildKit RUN mounts/network/security/device controls. Stable Dockerfile syntax and BuildKit entitlement/configuration support vary; labs features are explicitly experimental.",
        "HEALTHCHECK --start-interval requires Docker Engine 25.0+. Health metadata alone does not make the engine restart a container merely because it is unhealthy. Docker Engine/CLI, Buildx, BuildKit, Dockerfile frontend, and Compose have separate release versions and must be checked independently.",
        "Docker Content Trust and Notary v1 are being retired; Docker documentation currently gives 2026-12-08 as the Notary v1 service shutdown date. Explain DCT as legacy terminology and teach current image signing/attestation verification options under an explicit trust policy."
      ],
